## What it is

Cosori's first automatic pour-over, released in summer 2026 after a Kickstarter. A retractable nozzle traces one of three pour patterns while the basket rotates underneath it, over a V60-style cone. It's on the SCA's 2026 list of certified home brewers.

- **Grinder:** none. You'll need your own, which matters if you're comparing it to the machines that grind for you.
- **Capacity:** up to 1.5L in a thermal carafe, so it can brew a full pot, unlike the single-cup machines
- **Controls:** a touch panel on the machine, plus the VeSync app. There are one-touch presets and a feature that suggests a recipe when you scan a bag of beans.
- **Temperature:** 176–205°F
- **Warranty:** 2 years

## In the video

In [One Of These Coffee Robots Just Beat Keurig](https://youtu.be/En-YPVqqr6k), Daddy Got Coffee tests it alongside the xBloom Studio and Breville Spiral Luxe. It's the only one of the three without a grinder, and the cheapest by about $300.

## Worth knowing

Written reviews like the value and consistency, but they point out that it's almost all plastic, with a lot of moving parts. On the Home-Barista forum, some owners question whether the water gets hot enough. Cosori says the finished cup meets SCA temperature guidelines. It's a first-generation machine, so there's no track record yet.
